            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JUnit Jupiter provides robust support for handling test exceptions. This includes the built-in mechanisms for managing test failures due to exceptions, the role of exceptions in implementing assertions and assumptions, and how to specifically assert non-throwing conditions in code."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In JUnit Jupiter, if an exception is thrown from a test method, a lifecycle method, or an extension and not caught within that test method, lifecycle method, or extension, the framework will mark the test or test class as failed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Failed assumptions deviate from this general rule."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "In contrast to failed assertions, failed assumptions do not result in a test failure; rather, a failed assumption results in a test being aborted."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "See "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "writing-tests/assumptions.html"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "xref",
                    "target": "writing-tests/assumptions.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " for further details and examples."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "tip"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the following example, the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "failsDueToUncaughtException()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " method throws an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ArithmeticException"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Since the exception is not caught within the test method, JUnit Jupiter will mark the test as failed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "dlist",
                "id": null,
                "items": [
                  {
                    "description": {
                      "blocks": [
                        {
                          "blocks": [
                            {
                              "context": "listing",
                              "id": null,
                              "inlines": [
                                {
                                  "kind": "text",
                                  "value": "private final Calculator calculator = new Calculator();\n\n@Test\nvoid failsDueToUncaughtException() {\n\t// The following throws an ArithmeticException due to division by\n\t// zero, which causes a test failure.\n\tcalculator.divide(1, 0);\n}"
                                }
                              ],
                              "language": "java",
                              "roles": [],
                              "title": null
                            }
                          ],
                          "context": "open",
